[test-suite name=sched ring=1
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/sched (spec/02-working/stdlib_sched.md
§3/§6/§10). Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
(resolver MUST be quoted). The LAST expression is the rendered result.

   sched is a durable scheduler: after / at / every (fixed-delay|fixed-rate) /
   recur (a time [recurrence …] rule) / cron, cancel, durable timers
   (journal-backed, survive restart via restore), a catch-up policy
   (on-missed), and a controllable :manual test clock. It COMPOSES three
   shipped modules (time recurrence math, journal durability, the picoev loop)
   and adds NO calendar grammar, NO persistence, and NO new capability (§0/§5).

   FOUR-CHANNEL MODEL (code.md §9.1.2): an armed/fired/canceled timer is a
   present [timer] VALUE; a bad arg/mode/durable is an [err] in CXER4970-4989;
   COUNT/UNTIL exhaustion is the NORMAL terminal "fired" transition (a value,
   not a fault); an orphaned durable intent on restore is a present finding in
   the [restore-report …] VALUE, never silently dropped.

   HERMETIC. ALL fixtures run under the :manual test clock (§3.3) — this
   evaluator loop is the conformance harness loop and runs :manual by default,
   so virtual-now starts at the epoch (instant 0). Timers fire only when
   [$sched:test-clock-advance] moves virtual time past their deadline, in
   deadline order, deterministically and SLEEP-FREE (§4.2). NO wall-clock
   sleeps; NO nondeterministic values asserted. `at`/`recur`/`cron` fixtures
   use EPOCH-anchored datetimes (1970-01-01…) so a small advance crosses them.

   FIRING is one of two effects chosen by $ev's shape (§2.1): a zero-arg
   callable ([?fn [] …]) is invoked on the loop (its return ignored); a
   [?channel] value gets a [tick timer=<name>] posted to its queue — the
   fixtures observe a fire by [?receive]-ing that tick. A raw effect in a fired
   callback without a live grant hits CXER0271 at the callback's effect point;
   the fixture surfaces it by [?send]-ing the effect's result to a channel.

   on-missed (§2.5/§4.6): a single test-clock-advance that crosses N occurrences
   applies the policy exactly as a real fast-forward would — :skip fires once
   (the latest), :coalesce fires once, :fire-all fires once per crossed
   occurrence. A continuous occurrence-by-occurrence advance under :fire-all
   observes every tick (the recur COUNT-3 path).

   Error band CXER4970-4989 (§8): 4970 test-clock-under-wall (pinned by §7
   footnote 1; UNREACHABLE from the public surface in this :manual loop — the
   wall-clock production loop is the synthetic-transport part, gate=pending),
   4971 arg-invalid, 4972 mode/on-missed invalid, 4973 durable-no-name, 4974
   durable-no-journal, 4975 restore-intent-corrupt. Shared: CXER0271 (effect
   denial in a fired callback). cron parse faults surface time's CXER33xx
   unchanged (NOT a sched code).

   Id ranges:
     001-009  after / at / every / cancel / state / clock-mode / with-open
     010-016  recur / cron + COUNT/UNTIL terminal + fixed-rate cadence
     017-021  on-missed catch-up (skip / coalesce / fire-all)
     022-027  durable / restore (worker-recycle correctness) + orphaned
     028-036  negatives (CXER4971-4975 + CXER0271 + cron parse fault)
   #]]

  [# ── 001-009: after / at / every / cancel / state / clock-mode / with-open ── #]

  [case id=sched-001-after-fires-once level=core
   [tags sched after channel tick state]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="ticks" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:after [$time:duration-m 10] $ch]]
[= $s0 [$sched:timer-state $t]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 10]]]
[seq $s0 [$sched:timer-state $t] [?receive from=$ch]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'armed' 'fired' [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-002-after-callback-side-effect level=core
   [tags sched after callable fn fire]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $cb [?fn [] [?send "ding" to=$ch]]]
[= $t [$sched:after [$time:duration-m 10] $cb]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 10]]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] [?receive from=$ch]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'fired' 'ding']
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-003-cancel-before-fire level=core
   [tags sched cancel armed prevented]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:after [$time:duration-m 10] $ch]]
[= $c [$sched:cancel $t]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 10]]]
[seq $c [$sched:timer-state $t]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq true 'canceled']
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-004-cancel-after-fire-idempotent level=core
   [tags sched cancel fired idempotent false]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:after [$time:duration-m 10] $ch]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 10]]]
[$sched:cancel $t]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
false
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-005-clock-mode-manual level=core
   [tags sched clock-mode manual pure]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[$sched:clock-mode]
#]]
   [out-text [#
':manual'
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-006-at-future-fires level=core
   [tags sched at absolute one-shot datetime]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:at [$time:datetime 1970 1 1 0 10 0] $ch]]
[= $s0 [$sched:timer-state $t]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 10]]]
[seq $s0 [$sched:timer-state $t] [?receive from=$ch]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'armed' 'fired' [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-007-at-past-fires-next-turn level=core
   [tags sched at past one-shot]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:at [$time:datetime 1969 12 31 0 0 0] $ch]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-s 1]]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] [?receive from=$ch]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'fired' [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-008-every-fires-n-stays-armed level=core
   [tags sched every recurring fixed-delay armed]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=16]]
[= $t [$sched:every [$time:duration-m 1] $ch]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 5]]]
[= $a [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $b [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $c [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $d [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $e [?receive from=$ch]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] $a $b $c $d $e]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'armed' [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-009-with-open-cancels-on-exit level=core
   [tags sched with-open closeable cancel]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $saved [?with-open [$sched:after [$time:duration-m 10] $ch] $t $t]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 10]]]
[$sched:timer-state $saved]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
'canceled'
#]]
  ]

  [# ── 010-016: recur / cron + COUNT/UNTIL terminal + fixed-rate ── #]

  [case id=sched-010-recur-count-3-fires-3-terminal level=core
   [tags sched recur recurrence count terminal fire-all]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=16]]
[= $r [$time:recurrence :daily '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z' 'UTC' {count: 3}]]
[= $t [$sched:recur $r $ch {on-missed: :fire-all}]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-d 10]]]
[= $a [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $b [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $c [?receive from=$ch]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] $a $b $c]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'fired' [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-011-recur-state-armed-between level=core
   [tags sched recur armed between occurrences]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=16]]
[= $r [$time:recurrence :daily '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z' 'UTC' {count: 3}]]
[= $t [$sched:recur $r $ch]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-h 12]]]
[$sched:timer-state $t]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
'armed'
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-012-recur-no-future-terminal-at-arm level=core
   [tags sched recur until exhausted terminal arm]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $r [$time:recurrence :daily '1960-01-01T00:00:00Z' 'UTC' {count: 1}]]
[= $t [$sched:recur $r $ch]]
[$sched:timer-state $t]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
'fired'
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-013-cron-valid-fires level=core
   [tags sched cron parse fires]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:cron "0 0 * * *" $ch]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-d 1]]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] [?receive from=$ch]]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'armed' [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-014-every-fixed-rate-on-grid level=core
   [tags sched every fixed-rate grid cadence]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=16]]
[= $t [$sched:every [$time:duration-m 1] $ch {mode: :fixed-rate}]]
[= $a0 [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 1]]]
[= $a [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $b0 [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 1]]]
[= $b [?receive from=$ch]]
[= $c0 [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 1]]]
[= $c [?receive from=$ch]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] $a $b $c]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[seq 'armed' [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1] [tick timer=timer-1]]
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-015-after-zero-advance-no-fire level=core
   [tags sched after no-advance armed]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $t [$sched:after [$time:duration-m 10] $ch]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-m 5]]]
[$sched:timer-state $t]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
'armed'
#]]
  ]

  [case id=sched-016-recur-count-1-anchor-future level=core
   [tags sched recur count one occurrence]
   [in-cx [# [empty] #]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?let [= $ch [?channel name="t" buffer=4]]
[= $r [$time:recurrence :daily '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z' 'UTC' {count: 1}]]
[= $t [$sched:recur $r $ch {on-missed: :fire-all}]]
[= $_ [$sched:test-clock-advance [$time:duration-d 5]]]
[seq [$sched:timer-state $t] [?receive from=$ch]]]
#]]
